    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-5069",
      "problem": "What are the lengths of the major and semi-major axes of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275040/assets/21566535aac6e5e45f10c1b2edec4d58f5a3921dc6a409f900b355e7eb066dad.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The major axis is the longest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(-2,-5)$ and $(-2,3).$ So, the length of the major axis is $3-(-5)=8.$\n\nThe length of the semi-major axis is half the length of the major axis. So, the length of the semi-major axis $\\dfrac{8}{2} = 4.$",
